BEGIN_HYPERDESC
<h1>TRAPPIST-1 e: on the shore</h1>
A delta-glider on the lowlands of TRAPPIST-1 e, 40 light years away, near the
edge of the open sea that lies under its red dwarf. The planet is tidally
locked: the star stands still in its amber sky, and the other planets of the
system pass by, some larger than the Moon in Earth's sky.<br>
Its size, mass and orbit are measured; its surface, ocean and atmosphere are
assumed (procedural).
END_HYPERDESC

